Experiment 12: Develop a  program to stimulate interfacing with the keypad module to record the keystrokes



AIM: To develop a program for interfacing a matrix keypad module with arduino to detect and record keystrokes.

 
COMPONENTS:
 


Sl. No.     Quantity     Component

1              1                   Arduino Uno R3

2              1                  USB Cable

3              1                  4 x 4 Matrix Keypad

4              8                  Jumper Wires
 






CIRCUIT DIAGRAM:

 
 


SETUP:

a) Connect the 4×4 matrix keypad module to the Arduino Uno as per the circuit diagram. b) Ensure VCC and GND connections are properly made to avoid damage to the Arduino board.
c) Connect the Arduino Uno to the computer using the USB cable.
d) Open Arduino IDE, then go to Tools → Board and select Arduino Uno.
e) In Tools → Port, select the COM port to which the Arduino board is connected. f) Type the keypad interfacing program (sketch) in Arduino IDE.
g) Compile and Upload the program to transfer it to the Arduino board.
h) Open Serial Monitor in Arduino IDE to view the recorded keystrokes.

CODE:

#include <Keypad.h>

const byte numRows= 4; //number of rows on the keypad const byte numCols= 4; //number of columns on the keypad
//keymap defines the key pressed according to the row and columns just as appears on the keypad

char keymap[numRows][numCols]=

{

{'1', '2', '3', 'A'},

{'4', '5', '6', 'B'},

{'7', '8', '9', 'C'},

{'*', '0', '#', 'D'}

};

//Code that shows the the keypad connections to the arduino terminals byte rowPins[numRows] = {9,8,7,6}; //Rows 0 to 3
byte colPins[numCols]= {5,4,3,2}; //Columns 0 to 3

//initializes an instance of the Keypad class

Keypad   myKeypad=   Keypad(makeKeymap(keymap),   rowPins,   colPins,   numRows, numCols);
 



void setup()

{ Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop()

{

char keypressed = myKeypad.getKey();

if (keypressed != NO_KEY)

{ Serial.println(keypressed);
}

}

RESULT:

Successfully executed a program for interfacing a matrix keypad module with arduino to detect and record keystrokes.
